Hub OS P11: the session file and the runtime state file are written by a worker thread (never on the event loop), so a stalled disk
cannot freeze the compositor. Only the newest bytes per file are kept while the worker is stuck. The IPC `state` reply (and `driftwm msg state`)
gains two numbers: failed_writes (writes that ended with an error) and pending_writes (waiting or in progress; a number that never goes down
means a stuck disk). JSON: two new keys with serde defaults; text output: two new last lines `failed-writes N` and `pending-writes N`.

